<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<list xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="xsd/VillageSiege.xsd">
	<!--
		Village Under Siege (config/Custom/VillageSiege.ini): one village after the other, monsters of the
		hunting grounds around a starting village or a town attack its entrances. The defenders hold the gate of each
		entrance with the village guards, and contribution is paid in Defence Medals. Defenders above the levels below
		get monsters of their own level (VillageSiegeScaleToDefenders).

		village
		  id             the key used in VillageSiegeOrder and by //villagesiege
		  name           shown in announcements and on the Defence Force Board
		  town           the name of the village's TownZone (data/zones/custom_town.xml)
		  gatekeeper     the village gatekeeper npc: the heart of the village, and the Defence Force Board stands near it
		  guardLook      the npc whose look the siege guards borrow (one of the village's own guards)
		  minLevel       optional: the levels of the siege's monsters, from minLevel to maxLevel. They are the monsters
		  maxLevel       of those levels living nearest the village (on the entrance's road, around the village, farther
		                 out, or anywhere). The siege guards are a few levels above the middle (VillageSiegeGuardLevelOffset).
		                 By default VillageSiegeLevelWindow around the average level of the monsters living around it.
		  minDefenderLevel optional: the levels of the characters the siege is for, who hear of it, are invited, can
		  maxDefenderLevel take its teleport and earn contribution. By default 1 to VillageSiegeMaxPlayerLevel (and its
		                 announcements reach VillageSiegeAnnounceMaxLevel).

		entrance (optional) a fixed entrance: the gate stands at x, y, z, and the waves form at rallyX, rallyY,
		  rallyZ (optional; by default straight out from the village). Without any, the entrances are found on their own:
		  the roads the monsters of the hunting grounds around take into the village (where a path from out on their side
		  crosses into the TownZone). //villagesiege entrances <id> shows them, with lines to paste here to keep them.
		  The villages below whose roads climb ramps or cross heights the search can't follow have theirs set here, at
		  the posts of their retail gate guards.
	-->
	<village id="talking_island" name="Talking Island Village" town="Talking Island" gatekeeper="30006" guardLook="30039" minLevel="8" maxLevel="12" />
	<village id="elven" name="Elven Village" town="Elven Village" gatekeeper="30146" guardLook="30216" minLevel="8" maxLevel="12">
		<entrance x="45632" y="46522" z="-2992" /> <!-- North: Sentinels Wheeler and Berros -->
		<entrance x="47498" y="51666" z="-2992" /> <!-- East: Sentinels Kendell and Veltress -->
		<entrance x="42891" y="51255" z="-2992" /> <!-- West: Sentinels Starden and Rayen -->
	</village>
	<village id="dark_elven" name="Dark Elven Village" town="Dark Elven Village" gatekeeper="30134" guardLook="30346" minLevel="8" maxLevel="12">
		<entrance x="7570" y="17718" z="-4376" rallyX="6490" rallyY="19761" rallyZ="-3688" /> <!-- West: the ramp down from the south-west guards -->
		<entrance x="15196" y="15983" z="-4376" rallyX="17204" rallyY="13297" rallyZ="-3732" /> <!-- East: the ramp down from the north-east guards -->
	</village>
	<village id="orc" name="Orc Village" town="Orc Village" gatekeeper="30576" guardLook="30577" minLevel="8" maxLevel="12">
